  "_id": "6a7f5797757ee51246381bfb",
  "lab": "6a7f5796eda1a5feaff0b458",
  "name": "Free Testosterone ",
  "code": "FREE TESTOS",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<p><br></p><ul><li>A free testosterone test measures the amount of testosterone that is not bound to proteins in the blood. The interpretation of free testosterone levels can vary depending on individual factors, such as age and gender, as well as the reason for the test.&nbsp;</li><li><strong>Normal range:</strong> The normal range for free testosterone levels in adult males is typically between 9 and 30 ng/dL. In adult females, the normal range is typically between 0.3 and 1.9 ng/dL.&nbsp;</li><li><strong>Low levels:</strong> Low levels of free testosterone can be caused by a variety of factors, including aging, certain medications, and medical conditions such as hypogonadism. Symptoms of low testosterone levels can include fatigue, low libido, erectile dysfunction, and muscle weakness.&nbsp;</li><li><strong>High levels:</strong> High levels of free testosterone can be caused by medical conditions such as polycystic ovary syndrome (PCOS) or congenital adrenal hyperplasia (CAH). In females, high levels of testosterone can cause symptoms such as acne, excess hair growth, and irregular menstrual cycles.\n<br>​<br></li></ul>",
